---A type of OutputConfig, used when the output in a feed is for the smart subtitling feature. Smart subtitling uses automatic speech recognition (ASR) to generate live TTML subtitles from the audio in your source media.
---@class aws.elementalinference.SubtitlingConfig
---@field language aws.elementalinference.TranscriptionLanguage|string The language of the audio in the source media. Elemental Inference uses this setting to optimize transcription accuracy. Specify the language using an ISO 639-2/T three-letter code, optionally with a region subtag. Supported values: eng, eng-au, eng-gb, eng-us, fra, ita, deu, spa, por.
---@field aspectRatio? aws.elementalinference.AspectRatio The aspect ratio of the output video, specified as width and height integer values. Elemental Inference uses the aspect ratio to determine subtitle layout and line lengths.
---@field dictionary? aws.elementalinference.DictionaryId The ID of a custom dictionary to improve transcription accuracy for domain-specific terminology. Use the CreateDictionary operation to create a dictionary.
---@field profanityFilter? aws.elementalinference.ProfanityFilterMode|string Controls how profanity is handled in the generated subtitles. Valid values: DISABLED (no filtering, default), CENSOR (replace profanity with asterisks), DROP (remove profanity from the transcript).

---@alias aws.elementalinference.SummaryGenerationMode "ENABLED"|"DISABLED"

